# Regenerable products of a local run: the generated AIR, the linked metallib,
# the compiled dispatch host, and the manifest the driver hands the host.
# `tile_width_sweep.py --work-dir` writes all of it and rebuilds all of it; the
# evidence is the TSVs under `results/`, which stay tracked.
#
# The rule covers this one directory and nothing broader. Passing a --work-dir
# outside the repository puts the same products there instead, which is what the
# frozen commands do on the bench host.
/work/
/results-timing/
__pycache__/
